# African Drumming Classes at Solbar.

[![African Drumming Classes at Solbar](/media/2013/10/solbar_logo.jpg)](/the-solbar-and-rhythm-culture-presents-african-drumming-classes-with-nathaniel-combs/solbar_logo/) Do you want to have fun? Do you want to find your rhythm? This month Rhythm Culture and Solbar present African drumming classes. Did you know [new research](http://gazzaleylab.ucsf.edu/gazzaley-hart-collaboration.html) shows that rhythm is fundamental to how the brain works and good rhythm promotes good health both physically and mentally leading to longer, happier lives\*. "I have been teaching and facilitating drumming classes and workshops for almost 10 years. Rhythm is contagious and everyone can do it, so come and join in the fun!" - Nathaniel Combs Book your 5 week course BEFORE Oct 13 and receive your first class FREE! $79.00 (save $21) Contact us now! Starts Wednesday 16th October 4:45-5:45pm These classes are for everyone! All levels of African Drumming are welcome including  beginners with no previous experience to intermediate and experienced players. Families are also welcome with children 8+.  The focus for these classes will be technique and all the different parts that make African rhythms so groovy and contagious. Students will be introduced to African instruments and will have the opportunity to explore their own style and musical creativity in a relaxed and fun environment. So come play with us and get into some rhythm culture!
